1	# OpenAI SDK Knowledge MCP Server (unofficial)
2	
3	[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
4	[![TypeScript](https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-007ACC?logo=typescript&logoColor=white)](https://www.typescriptlang.org/)
5	[![Cloudflare Workers](https://img.shields.io/badge/Cloudflare-Workers-F38020?logo=cloudflare&logoColor=white)](https://workers.cloudflare.com/)
6	
7	An MCP server that knows the OpenAI API inside and out. 100% TypeScript built with [OpenAI Agents SDK](https://openai.github.io/openai-agents-js/), [Hono](https://hono.dev), Cloudflare Workers, and [Drizzle ORM](https://orm.drizzle.team/). Powered by RAG and ready to answer your technical questions.
8	
9	<img width="600" alt="website" src="./public/images/readme_website.png" />
10	
11	## Developer Highlights
12	
13	- **Cloudflare stack**: Fully leverages Cloudflare Workers, Queues, D1, Vectorize, and AI Gateway.
14	- **Streamable HTTP MPC Server**: Compatible with any MPC clients.
15	- **ChatGPT Deep Research connector**: Meets ChatGPT's Deep Research connector requirements.
16	- **Always updated**: Continuously fetches OpenAI repos and community forums for new content.
17	- **Rapidly built with AI**: Developed hand in hand with various AI coding tools.
18	
19	## Streamable HTTP MCP Server
20	
21	Use a publicly accessible URL (e.g., ngrok, Cloudflare Tunnel) to serve the endpoints for MCP clients. You can generate the token on the top page:
22	
23	```json
24	{
25	  "mcpServers": {
26	    "openai-sdk-knowledge.org": {
27	      "type": "streamable-http",
28	      "url": "https://openai-sdk-knowledge.org/mcp",
29	      "headers": {
30	        "Authorization": "Bearer {your api key here}"
31	      }
32	    }
33	  }
34	}
35	```
36	
37	For example, you can add this MCP server to Cursor:
38	
39	<img width="600" alt="Cursor MCP server" src="./public/images/readme_cursor_mcp.png" />
40	
41	Not only Cursor—you can use this MCP server with any other tools supporting MCP server connections.
42	
43	### OpenAI Responses API's Hosted MCP Server Tool
44	
45	You can pass `https://openai-sdk-knowledge.org/mcp` along with a valid API token:
46	
47	<img width="300" src="./public/images/readme_playground_1.png" /><img width="300" src="./public/images/readme_playground_2.png" />
48	
49	Then, you can call the tool in the conversation with the Responses API agent:
50	
51	<img width="600" src="./public/images/readme_playground_3.png" />
52	
53	### ChatGPT Deep Research MCP Connector
54	
55	Also, for ChatGPT Deep Research customer connector, use the same URL. When the ChatGPT server accesses this app's MCP server endpoint, it returns `search` and `fetch` tools as well (see [the documentation](https://platform.openai.com/docs/mcp) for details).
56	
57	<img width="600" alt="Use the connector in Deep Research" src="./public/images/readme_chatgpt_deep_research.png" />
58	
59	## Run Locally
60	
61	```bash
62	# Clone and install
63	git clone https://github.com/seratch/openai-sdk-knowledge-org.git
64	cd openai-sdk-knowledge-org/
65	npm install
66	
67	# Configure (add your OpenAI API key)
68	cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
69	# Edit .dev.vars: OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here
70	
71	# Run it
72	npm run dev
73	```
74	
75	You can access `http://localhost:8787` and see how it works.
76	
77	**Requirements**: Node.js 22+ and API keys (OpenAI, GitHub)
78	
79	## Architecture
80	
81	This app is essentially a simple web app that runs on Cloudflare Workers. The web app provides MCP server protocol compatible endpoints, as well as a web user interface. For the RAG data pipeline, it collects data from sources and generates asynchronous tasks to run and enqueue them into Cloudflare’s Queue.
82	
83	```
84	src/
85	├── agents/          # Internally used agents built with OpenAI Agents SDK
86	├── pipeline/        # RAG data collection and processing
87	├── server/mcp/      # MCP protocol implementation
88	├── server/web/      # Web app implementation
89	├── storage/         # Vector database (Vectorize) and D1 database access
90	└── index.ts         # App entry point
91	```
92	
93	<img width="600" src="./public/images/readme_architecture.png" />
94	
95	## License
96	
97	MIT
98	

